  "_comment": "Single source of truth for monokernel shapes. Each entry declares ONE compile-time specialization (the kernel is template-specialized on N/K/E, so a new shape needs a rebuild). The generator csrc/moe/moe_monokernel/tools/gen_shapes.py reads this and emits the C++ Dims structs / wrapper impls / op decls / torch bindings (as *.inc include files) plus the Python dispatch table. Shape-keyed op names are E{E}_N{N}_K{K}; legacy 35B/122B names are kept as aliases for back-compat. config[0] MUST be the shipped default (its knobs define the base Dims). UP_COL_HALVES is DERIVED from DCT: uch = max(1, 2*N*DCT/(128*K)); uch>=2 => raw two-TMA up-proj (no Python interleave). top_k is a RUNTIME arg (1..8); the value here is only the tuner/serving default.",
